\section{Modelling Churn Risk}

\subsection{Candidates, tuning and selection}

Three model families were trained on the same inputs: \textbf{logistic regression} (the interpretable baseline), a \textbf{random forest} (the required tree-based model) and \textbf{XGBoost} gradient boosting (stretch). Each was tuned by << cfg.cv_folds >>-fold stratified cross-validation on the training split with average precision (PR-AUC) as the objective, because churners are a minority and the business cares about the top of the ranking \cite{saito2015}. Each tuned model was then calibrated with a sigmoid (Platt) mapping fitted on out-of-fold predictions \cite{platt1999,niculescu2005}. A prior-only model, which predicts the churn rate for everyone, anchors the metrics.

