\textbf{Break-even.} The base-budget list breaks even at a standard-offer save rate of \textbf{<< be.break_even_default_save_rate | pct >>} or at offer costs << be.offer_cost_multiplier | ratio(2) >> today's; the larger recommended list breaks even at \textbf{<< rbe_std | pct >>}, because its additional customers have lower expected value. Both figures scale every offer's save rate in proportion and are expressed as the standard offer's rate; measured as the average save rate of the recommended offer mix, which is what a pilot observes, the break-even is << rbe | pct >> against an assumed << qmix | pct >>. Below a standard-offer save rate of << be.minimum_viable_save_rate | pct >> no customer-offer pair has a positive EV and the right decision is not to run a campaign.

