\section{Fairness, Ethics and Customer Experience}

<% set senior = fairness_by[strategy ~ '|SeniorCitizen|1'] %><% set senior_risk = fairness_by['risk|SeniorCitizen|1'] %><% set female = fairness_by[strategy ~ '|gender|Female'] %>
Gender and age are not model inputs, but they are used to audit \emph{who receives offers} \cite{barocas2023}. Selection-rate ratios outside << cfg.guardrails.selection_ratio_alert[0] >>--<< cfg.guardrails.selection_ratio_alert[1] >> (the ``four-fifths'' screening analogy \cite{cfr1607}) are flagged for human review rather than corrected automatically (Figure~\ref{fig:fair}).

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Senior citizens} are contacted << senior.ratio_to_reference | ratio(2) >> as often as other customers under the recommended rule (<< senior_risk.ratio_to_reference | ratio(2) >> under risk-only targeting). Adjusted for risk decile the ratio falls to << senior.risk_adjusted_ratio | ratio(2) >>: higher churn risk explains part of the gap and higher bills (value) the rest. Being selected means receiving both a discount and a call, so the gap is a benefit and a burden at once; it is flagged for review by Legal/DPO in every wave.
  \item \textbf{Gender:} ratio << female.ratio_to_reference | ratio(2) >> (95\% interval << female.ratio_lower_95 | num(2) >>--<< female.ratio_upper_95 | num(2) >>), within normal variation.
  \item \textbf{Loyalty penalty:} long-tenure and contract customers are rarely contacted because their risk is low. To avoid the perception that only those who threaten to leave are rewarded \cite{cma2020}, the playbook recommends a non-targeted loyalty benefit funded outside the retention budget.
  \item \textbf{Contact burden and compliance:} at most << cfg.campaign.max_contact_share | pct(0) >> of customers per wave, one retention contact per 30 days, consent and do-not-call checks; in Vietnam, advertising calls are limited to 08:00--17:00 and one per subscriber per 24 hours \cite{decree91}, and personal data processing requires purpose-specific consent \cite{pdpl2025}.
\end{itemize}

